    [BugFix][Build] Package shared headers for standalone kernel compilation (#18602)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Installed custom OPP packages cannot compile some kernels after the
    original build checkout is removed. Generated adapters force-include
    cann_compat.h through a build-time absolute path, while Catlass/TLA and
    shared MoE kernel_utils headers are missing from the package.
    
    Use -includecann_compat.h and publish these dependencies into the
    package's existing ascendc/common include directory. A shared CMake
    install function keeps the regular and BUILD_OPS_RTY_KERNEL installation
    rules consistent. Stage cann_compat.h for local kernel builds; preserve
    existing operator source include paths and the Python adapter generator.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce any user-facing change?
    
    Installed packages carry the shared headers needed for standalone static
    kernel compilation. No public API or environment variable changes.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Built and installed a JIT package containing DispatchFFNCombine,
    Compressor, ChunkFwdOVllm, ChunkGatedDeltaRuleFwdHVllm, and
    MsaIndexScore on CANN 9.2.0 / Ascend910_9392 using GCC 13.
    - Confirmed the installed package contains cann_compat.h, 233
    Catlass/TLA files, and all five kernel_utils files.
    - Hid the source checkout's csrc directory and unset CPATH,
    CPLUS_INCLUDE_PATH, and C_INCLUDE_PATH. Static compilation passed for 16
    captured DispatchFFNCombine inputs, one captured Compressor input, one
    synthetic input for each Chunk operator, and one quantized MsaIndexScore
    input.
    - Repository pre-commit checks passed. No new unit tests are added.
    
    Validation limitation: BUILD_OPS_RTY_KERNEL configuration is blocked by
    the existing reference to the missing csrc/ffn directory. Its shared
    installation call was reviewed, but that branch was not built end to
    end. A Docker image was not rebuilt.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/c4df37dfcc7f72ca41cd43801a468526ecf99a2b
    
